"n":2863,"url":"https://github.com/kserve/kserve/issues/2863","title":"Allow using SSL between transformer and predictor","text":"Currently the transformer is hard-coded to [use `http` to communicate with the predictor](https://github.com/kserve/kserve/blob/master/python/kserve/kserve/model.py#L36). We should add an extra `use_ssl` property to the `Model` that will enable connecting to the predictor via HTTPS. By default this property would be `false`.","label":"feature","kind":{"bug":0.0051,"feature":0.9871,"question":0.0077},"area":["python",0.5007],"needs_info":0.0505,"priority":0.9352},{"n":2167,"url":"https://github.com/kserve/kserve/issues/2167","title":"How can Custom Predictors load models in model storage?","text":"I want to customize the predictor by putting the mar file in the model storage. [code] How do you load and use the model in the load method when you use the predictor for custom? For example, I want to load model of model store into `self.model` [code]","label":"question","kind":{"bug":0.0038,"feature":0.0123,"question":0.9839},"area":["storage",0.6014],"needs_info":0.4192,"priority":0.7482},{"n":2548,"url":"https://github.com/kserve/kserve/issues/2548","title":"Istio 503","text":"I make an image myself and deploy it through KServe, but when I access isvc through istio, istio gives a 503 status code. The specific error is [code] I want to be able to access my isvc through istio When I used KFServing 0.6.1 before, it was working fine. When I upgraded KFServing to KServe 0.9.0rc, it gave the above error. - Istio Version: 1.9.4 - Knative Version: v1.4.0 - KFServing Version: 0.9.0rc - Kfdef:[k8s_i\u2026","label":"bug","kind":{"bug":0.4958,"feature":0.0083,"question":0.4958},"area":["networking",0.8638],"needs_info":0.7678,"priority":1.6098},{"n":3763,"url":"https://github.com/kserve/kserve/issues/3763","title":"Can't find version compatibility matrix for KServe","text":"I am trying to find compatibility matrix for KServe + K8S + KNative. There is thi